<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!--
        A couple of empty wallets, so the screen and its movements dialog can
        be seen on a shop where nobody has topped up yet.

        Deliberately no balances and no payments. A seeded balance is money the
        shop would owe a real customer and would show under "Money we hold"; a
        seeded payment would land in today's takings, the success rate and the
        sparkline, on the screen staff use to check the bank. An empty wallet
        is not a claim about money - it is what every customer starts with.

        In Python rather than as records, because a wallet needs a real partner
        and this module ships none. Not noupdate: the method guards itself and
        does nothing once any wallet exists, so running on every upgrade seeds
        exactly once.
    -->
    <data>
        <function model="loyalty.card" name="_mart369_load_demo"/>
    </data>
</odoo>
